   *
   *  `TabBar` has implemented `onAdd`/`onClose`/`onRename` since the console chrome needed them, and
   *  Screen simply never forwarded them — so every WORKSPACE tab strip was read-only while the console's
   *  was not. Forwarding costs three props and is what lets a tab set be a user's collection (Glance's
   *  networks) rather than a constant. */
  onAdd?: () => void;
  /** Close one page. Renders `TabBar`'s per-tab close affordance. */
  onClose?: (id: string) => void;
  /** Rename one page — `TabBar` drives this from a double-click, commits on Enter/blur, and drops an
   *  empty name, so a consumer never has to re-implement inline editing. */
  onRename?: (id: string, name: string) => void;
